 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Relative affine-line weight step",
 "statement": "For the projection $p:\\mathbf A^1_{Y_0}\\to Y_0$ and every\n$K\\in D_{\\le w}(\\mathbf A^1_{Y_0})$, one has\n$Rp_!K\\in D_{\\le w}(Y_0)$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-thm-dl-general-sheaf/thm-zl-relative-line-step.md",
  "place": "node thm-zl-relative-line-step, order 2848"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-weil-complex-weights",
  "def-weil-pbc-qbar-category"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "By [lem-zl-sheaves-to-complexes], it suffices to treat a mixed\nsheaf of weights at most $w$. Its finite weight filtration and the\nextension bounds of [lem-a1-extension-bounds]\n(propagated through the long exact sequences) reduce to a pure graded\npiece. Apply [thm-zl-relative-line-stratification]: on a\nrelative-curve stratum the assertion is\n[thm-zl-relative-affine-curve-core] (which gives the sheaf-level\nbound $R^ap_!\\mathcal F$ mixed of weights at most $w+a$, for pure\n$\\mathcal F$); on a quasi-finite stratum it is\n[lem-zl-quasi-finite]. The composition constraint\n[lem-zl-shriek-composition] identifies these stratumwise direct\nimages with the corresponding pieces of $Rp_!$. Noetherian induction,\nusing the one-way localization gluing rule [lem-zl-open-closed-weight]\nfor an open–closed decomposition of the strata, in the morphism-level\nform [lem-zl-morphism-open-closed-reduction], reassembles the source\nand target strata.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-zl-sheaves-to-complexes",
    "lem-a1-extension-bounds",
    "thm-zl-relative-line-stratification",
    "thm-zl-relative-affine-curve-core",
    "lem-zl-quasi-finite",
    "lem-zl-shriek-composition",
    "lem-zl-open-closed-weight",
    "lem-zl-morphism-open-closed-reduction"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
